  "known_limitations": [
    "Trained and evaluated only on QDAT's own fixed phrase set -- generalization to arbitrary Quran text the app's users actually recite is untested.",
    "Covers 3 of the SRS's ~4 Tajweed error categories (Separate Madd, Ghunnah, Ikhfa) -- no makhraj or general shaddah coverage; QDAT has no labeled data for those.",
    "QDAT's 'target' column was excluded -- its exact meaning was never confirmed against the original paper (network access to verify was unavailable).",
    "108/1,505 QDAT rows were exact-audio duplicates; 74 of those were a cross-speaker data-construction defect (different speaker metadata linked to identical audio), excluded from training entirely.",
    "Threshold calibration was done on 195 validation clips and confirmed NOT to transfer precisely to test: target was a 10% false-positive-on-correct rate, test came in at 12.1-12.4% for concealment/separate_tide -- a small-sample calibration limitation, documented rather than hidden.",
    "separate_tide (Separate Madd) is the weakest task (71-74% test accuracy). Root cause investigated: label noise among duplicates was tested and refuted; clip-duration signal was tested and confirmed (elongation duration is what the rule measures), improving accuracy from ~71% to ~74% when added as an input.",
    "This is a whole-clip classifier, not a real-time per-word detector -- QDAT has no word-level boundaries, so streaming/word-level highlighting (FR-7) needs a separate architectural extension, not just more training on this data."
  ],
